<title>USA: Lockheed tops U.S. defense contractors.</title>
<headline>Lockheed tops U.S. defense contractors.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aerospace giant Lockheed Martin Corp. last year again led all U.S. defense contractors with $12 billion in prime military contract awards, the Defense Department said on Friday.</p>
<p>In an annual list of firms ranked by prime contracting funds, Lockheed led in fiscal 1996 for the second consecutive year. It was followed by McDonnell Douglas Corp. with $9.9 billion in contracts, General Motors Corp.  with $3.2 billion, Raytheon Co. with $3 billion and General Dynamics Corp. with $2.7 billion.</p>
</text>
